How about a CAS loop which breaks when either we succeed in incrementing the value, or the value is >= `numRegisteredStore`? It would seem unfortunate to drop the trace on the floor only because someone raced with us.

As an alternative to this CAS (better, I think), consider:

```golang
if num := r.numRegisteredStore.Add(1); num > numAllowed {
	// This branch is super rare, considering all the checks above.
	// Only happens when multiple trace registers are racing when we
	// are about to exceed the limit.
	r.numRegisteredStore.Add(-1)
	return false
}
r.numRegisteredReplica.Add(1)
return true
```
